    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d320">

                <pb facs="0335" n="325" xml:id="pg325"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">840.48 Refugees/40365/6</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The British Ambassador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Halifax</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                        </hi><anchor n="91" xml:id="d320-f1"/>
                </head>
                <dateline>
                    <date ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-content" calendar="gregorian"
                        when="1943-07-13">undated</date>
                </dateline>
                <p>Following sent by Prime Minister to President on July 10th No. 357.</p>
                <p>I am most grateful to you for your number 308.<anchor n="92" xml:id="d320-f2"/>
                </p>
                <p>I am in complete accord with your suggestions, which will provide a solution for
                    our difficulties in Spain. As soon as I hear from you that you have issued the
                    directives to Generals Eisenhower and Giraud and to American Ambassador in
                    Madrid and Lisbon, I will give complementary instructions to our
                    authorities.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d320-f1" n="91" type="source" xml:id="d320-f1-content">
                <p>Transmitted to the Secretary of State by the British Ambassador in note dated
                    July 13, 1943.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d320-f2" n="92" xml:id="d320-f2-content">
